<title>USA: Whitman bottling unit president leaving.</title>
<headline>Whitman bottling unit president leaving.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Whitman Corp said Thursday William Frago, president and chief executive officer of its Pepsi-Cola General Bottlers unit, its largest subsidiary, is leaving the company, effective immediately.</p>
<p>No reason was given for Frago's resignation.</p>
<p>Whitman said Bruce Chelberg, chairman of Whitman, will assume the day-to-day responsibilities for Pepsi General until a successor to Frago is appointed.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
